WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:03.800
Speaker 1: Well, my friends, they did it,
this shouldn't even be notable.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:05.420
This shouldn't be newsworthy.

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.379
This shouldn't be a story.

00:00:07.379 --> 00:00:15.140
But 35 Republicans joined Democrats in the
House of Representatives to vote to pass a

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:23.730
bill that would set up this bipartisan 9/11
style commission to investigate the Donald

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:28.530
Trump, January 6th, insurrection riot.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:36.500
And it is incredible that it is only 35 members
from the Republican Party that joined one

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:39.730
hundred and seventy six Republicans or what?

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:40.730
No.

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:44.030
One seventy five, one seven one seventy five,
one hundred and seventy five Republicans.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:50.580
The vote was 252 to 175, saying we don't want
to know what happened and we don't want all

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:55.610
of these remaining questions answered in terms
of the motivations and the genesis and the

00:00:55.610 --> 00:01:01.149
explanation of why did it take so long to
get a bolstad police presence and the military,

00:01:01.149 --> 00:01:04.339
all of these different things that should
be investigated.

00:01:04.339 --> 00:01:12.200
They don't want to know or they believe that
it would point back to them in some way.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:17.240
This is the greatest motivation for these
Republicans not wanting this investigation,

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:23.040
which is that many of them know that it would
not look good for them.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:26.520
But we will get back to that Axios reporting.

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:33.280
As I told you yesterday, House Minority Leader
Kevin McCarthy opposed this commission and

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:38.340
it looked like there would be between 20 and
50 Republicans who would vote in favor of

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:41.490
it and 35 did.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:48.220
This makes it more difficult for Senate Minority
Leader Mitch McConnell to just dismiss it

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:53.280
all as partizan, because you did have 35 Republicans
in the House who were in favor of it.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:59.030
Now, as I told you yesterday, the setup is
really as bipartisan as you can get.

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:00.030
Democrats control the House.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:01.030
Yes.

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:05.320
So there is going to be some more control
that Democrats have rather than Republicans

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:06.430
over the commission.

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:11.969
But it would be a 10 member commission, five
members selected by Democrats, five members

00:02:11.969 --> 00:02:13.559
selected by Republicans.

00:02:13.559 --> 00:02:17.900
The chair would be a Democrat because Democrats
control the House and the vice chair would

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.110
be a Republican.

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:24.329
And if they are going to issue subpoenas,
which presumably they would, every subpoena

00:02:24.329 --> 00:02:27.719
has to be signed off on by the chair and the
vice chair.

00:02:27.719 --> 00:02:28.900
So there are Republicans.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:33.849
I mean, listen, if I'm Kevin McCarthy and
I realize that I was on the phone with Trump

00:02:33.849 --> 00:02:39.969
on the day of the insurrection, and the content
of that conversation may be of interest to

00:02:39.969 --> 00:02:43.689
the committee and I might be subpoenaed.

00:02:43.689 --> 00:02:48.290
That is going to be something that would require
both the Democratic chair and the Republican

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:50.349
vice chair.

00:02:50.349 --> 00:02:54.049
And indeed, there seems to be at least somewhat
of an appetite from Republicans to figure

00:02:54.049 --> 00:02:55.049
out what happened.

00:02:55.049 --> 00:03:00.380
And so if you're Kevin McCarthy and you're
thinking I might have to testify here, or

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:05.779
at least documents related to my conversation
with Trump might be part of this, it makes

00:03:05.779 --> 00:03:06.779
sense.

00:03:06.779 --> 00:03:07.859
You would try to make this go away.

00:03:07.859 --> 00:03:13.090
So the next step here, now that the House
has passed it, the Senate majority leader,

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:18.079
Chuck Schumer, Democrat from New York, has
said the bill will get a vote.

00:03:18.079 --> 00:03:22.779
It's not clear whether any Republicans in
the Senate are going to get on board.

00:03:22.779 --> 00:03:28.329
Two days ago, Mitch McConnell said he can't
support it in its then current form.

00:03:28.329 --> 00:03:34.729
Two sources say that it's conceivable that
Mitch McConnell will have to change his tune

00:03:34.729 --> 00:03:39.439
because of these 35 Republicans who voted
in favor of it, 10 Republican senators would

00:03:39.439 --> 00:03:40.999
be necessary for this to pass.

00:03:40.999 --> 00:03:47.079
You cannot pass this in the Senate with 50
plus Kamala Harris as the tie breaking vote.

00:03:47.079 --> 00:03:49.349
That would be the budget reconciliation process.

00:03:49.349 --> 00:03:50.549
It cannot be used here.

00:03:50.549 --> 00:03:54.709
So in order for this commission to happen,
for it to be voted through in the Senate,

00:03:54.709 --> 00:04:00.620
you will need all 50 Democrats and 10 Republicans
or 49 Democrats and 11 Republicans.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:01.750
Or you can do the math.

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:03.989
Any combination that gets you to 60.

00:04:03.989 --> 00:04:05.709
This could have started months ago.

00:04:05.709 --> 00:04:08.390
There was no interest before Joe Biden was
president.

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:11.349
There was not even the possibility before
Joe Biden was president because Democrats

00:04:11.349 --> 00:04:14.230
didn't didn't control the Senate.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:16.420
And now hopefully we are getting closer to
that.

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:17.859
It could have been done a long time ago.

00:04:17.859 --> 00:04:18.859
It really could.

00:04:18.859 --> 00:04:22.800
And it's because of Republicans and Republicans
only that it has not yet happened.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:25.020
So we're going to follow it.

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:29.770
And there are any number of different reasons
why different Republicans would want this

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:31.919
not to take place.

00:04:31.919 --> 00:04:38.289
But I would say I am more confident than I've
been in the last two weeks today that ultimately

00:04:38.289 --> 00:04:39.669
this is going to happen.

00:04:39.669 --> 00:04:45.090
And let's now look at some of the I don't
even really want to call them reasons because

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:49.520
they barely even have anything to do with
the actual commission and the riots.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:54.569
But let's look at some of the words that came
out of the mouths of Republicans during yesterday's

00:04:54.569 --> 00:06:15.240
debate about this on the floor 

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:29.630
of the House.

